# Security response headers for the Netlify deploy. This file is copied verbatim
# from web/public/ into dist/ at build, and Netlify applies it to every response.
# This is the ONE place the CSP lives — do not also add a [[headers]] block in
# netlify.toml: two CSP headers on the same response are each enforced by the
# browser (an intersection), and a stray netlify.toml block that predates the
# Google-sign-in origins below will silently break sign-in/webfonts by
# intersecting them back out. (That happened once — see CHANGELOG.)
#
# script/style/font/frame-src are containment: they only allow origins that
# map to real code (the Google Identity Services SDK + its auth iframe, and
# pdf.js's own WASM codec). Webfonts are self-hosted (web/public/fonts), so no
# third-party font or style ORIGIN is allowed. connect-src is deliberately
# OPEN — the BYO-AI agent endpoint and the optional /ai/* contribute path are
# user-configured to *any* origin (your own server, localhost, a local
# runtime) by design (see docs re: "AI-native, not a flooring freebie"), so it
# can't be pinned to a fixed allowlist here. That does mean an XSS could POST
# the signed-in user's Google access token to an arbitrary origin via fetch —
# a real trade-off, not an oversight. If you run team cloud mode WITHOUT the
# BYO-AI agent enabled, you can safely narrow connect-src to
# 'self' https://www.googleapis.com https://accounts.google.com for tighter
# token containment.
#
# Every allowed origin below maps to real code and was verified against the app:
#   script-src   'self'                         our bundle + /theme-init.js
#                'wasm-unsafe-eval'              pdf.js decodes embedded raster images
#                                               (JPEG2000/OpenJPEG) via WebAssembly;
#                                               verified — without it plans render
#                                               vector-only and raster images fail to
#                                               decode. This permits WASM compilation
#                                               ONLY, not JS eval(), so it does not
#                                               reopen the XSS hole 'unsafe-eval' would.
#                https://accounts.google.com     the Google Identity Services SDK
#   connect-src  *  data:  blob:                 open by design — see above
#   frame-src    https://accounts.google.com      the GIS auth iframe
#   img-src      'self' data: blob:               PDF thumbnails + logo/preview images
#   style-src    'self' 'unsafe-inline'          no third-party ORIGIN — webfonts are
#                                              self-hosted under web/public/fonts (see
#                                              web/src/styles/fonts.css). Do NOT re-add a
#                                              font CDN: that is a third-party request on
#                                              every page load. 'unsafe-inline' is
#                                              load-bearing (React inline styles) — the
#                                              directive is not, and cannot be, bare 'self'
#   worker-src   'self' blob:                     the bundled pdf.js worker
#   font-src     'self' data:                    'self' is our own woff2. `data:` is kept
#                                              for pdf.js, which can construct faces from
#                                              fonts embedded IN a plan PDF — it is NOT for
#                                              our webfonts. Grepping our source won't show
#                                              a data: font because the use is inside the
#                                              library; don't drop it on that evidence
#
# 'unsafe-inline' is intentionally absent from script-src — don't add it; it
# would undo the containment the other directives still provide.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://accounts.google.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self' data:; img-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src * data: blob:; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src https://accounts.google.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  # microphone=(self): push-to-talk dictation (RFC #59) — same-origin only,
  # audio is processed on-device in a Worker and never leaves the browser.
  # Everything else stays fully disabled.
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(self), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000

# Self-hosted webfonts. Deliberately NOT `immutable`: files under web/public/
# keep their authored names (Vite content-hashes only what it bundles from
# src/), so an immutable response would pin returning users to a stale font
# across a regeneration. A week is long enough to matter and short enough to
# recover from.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
